{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDIyL1RoZSUyMEphbmVzJTIwJTI4MjAyMiUyOS8","type":"movie","name":"The Janes","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/hKWJ0hw1tWOONaQliyrp2wC6Rcm.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/nQAfnJSH9kDxLi1pD9YxjeeG2rr.jpg","description":"Defying the state legislature that outlawed abortion, the Catholic Church that condemned it, and the Chicago Mob that was profiting from it, the members of “Jane” risked their personal and professional lives to support women with unwanted pregnancies. In the pre-Roe v. Wade era — a time when abortion was a crime in most states and even circulating information about abortion was a felony in Illinois — the Janes provided low-cost and free abortions to an estimated 11,000 women.\n\nReleased 3 May 2022 · United States of America · Language: English · 101 min\nStudio: HBO Documentary Films, Pentimento Productions, Elsewhere Films\n\nOn your server — Audio: English · Subtitle files: English","releaseInfo":"2022","genres":["Documentary","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"5.6","runtime":"101 min","cast":["Heather Booth","Judith Arcana","Marie Leaner","Diane Stevens","Eleanor Oliver","Martin Luther King Jr.","Walter Cronkite","Hugh Hefner"],"director":["Tia Lessin","Emma Pildes"],"released":"2022-05-03T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"They didn't have a choice.","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Tia Lessin","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/aVO7PXRKxMiv2bwm64J41hy9Msm.jpg"},{"name":"Heather Booth","character":"Self"},{"name":"Judith Arcana","character":"Self"},{"name":"Marie Leaner","character":"Self"},{"name":"Diane Stevens","character":"Self"},{"name":"Eleanor Oliver","character":"Self"},{"name":"Martin Luther King Jr.","character":"Self (archive footage)","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/bclVGQbWbPRQRC94e855oP4Inw0.jpg"},{"name":"Walter Cronkite","character":"Self (archive footage)","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/hCIBybvwP7